WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.940
Hey everyone, welcome to Tesla Short's Time, Daily Episode 506 for June 10th, 2026.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:08.920
I'm Patrick, coming to you from Vancouver.

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:11.660
Let's dive into today's Tesla news.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:17.800
Denmark's FSD Supervised Approval extends the system to four European countries

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:22.020
and shows how regulatory progress can outpace fleet deployment elsewhere.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:28.820
Tesla announced FSD Supervised Approvals in the Netherlands, Lithuania, Estonia, and Denmark.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:34.700
The company's stated rollout to Danish vehicle owners is expected to begin shortly after the June

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:39.960
9 announcement. This marks the fourth European country to clear the supervised system.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:46.380
Tesla released its first localized FSD Supervised Safety Snapshot for the Netherlands.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:51.880
The data covers how the system manages local roads, roundabouts, and right-of-way rules.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:58.160
Regulators are treating supervised operation as a distinct category rather than requiring full

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:02.940
autonomy from the start. While Europe moves forward on supervised features,

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:09.200
Tesla's actual Robotaxi deployment tells a different story. Tesla's Robotaxi operations

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:13.780
remain limited to 59 vehicles nearly a year after initial service began.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:19.680
The slow growth contrasts with earlier statements about rapid unsupervised expansion.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:24.960
Current operations stay confined to a narrow geographic area in Texas.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:30.560
The figure highlights the gap between software capability and actual scaled deployment.

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:36.160
Operations still limited to a narrow Texas area with minimal growth since launch.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:42.060
This connects directly to something we've been watching with CyberCab and Robotaxi since the last

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:47.480
update. Regulatory and deployment friction at the factory level adds another layer of pressure.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:52.980
The Bay Area Air Quality Management District issued 17 violations to the

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:58.360
free-mod factory on a single day. The citations relate to air emissions and permitting

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:04.100
requirements at the assembly plant. Tesla has not yet detailed corrective actions or whether

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:09.880
production was affected. The cluster of violations adds to ongoing scrutiny of the site's

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:15.660
environmental compliance record. The cluster raises questions about weather production schedules

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:21.320
are affecting compliance processes. Continued regulatory attention could add cost and

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:28.120
scheduling pressure at the main US assembly site. Meanwhile, Tesla is trying to regain momentum

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:34.680
in its largest single market. Tesla China sales rose 22% after two consecutive months of declines.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:40.020
The rebound follows price adjustments and new inventory allocations in the market.

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:45.680
It remains unclear whether the increase reflects sustained demand or temporary restocking.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:50.380
Monthly export and registration data will show if the uptick continues.

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:59.200
BYD captured 36.7% of China's May-NEV exports while Tesla held 9.1% for fourth place.

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:05.040
Tesla's share comes primarily from Shanghai-built vehicles shipped to Europe and other markets.

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:10.040
General Motors announced a partnership with Peak to enter stationary energy storage.

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:16.280
The move mirrors Tesla's Megapack business model of pairing vehicle production with grid-scale batteries.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:21.180
GM has not disclosed initial capacity targets or factory locations.

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:27.400
The entry adds another competitor in a segment where Tesla currently holds significant market share.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:33.520
A comparison of owner-reported reliability data shows Tesla vehicles ahead of Rivian models

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:39.900
across multiple categories. Analysis draws from warranty claims and roadside assistance records.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:44.760
Rivian has not released its own comparable long-term durability figures.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:50.120
The gap matters as both companies scale production and compete for the same buyer segment.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:56.500
Piper Sandler analysts stated Tesla has resolved core self-driving technical challenges.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:02.340
The firm cited recent FAD version performance and a regulatory traction as supporting evidence.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:06.780
No specific price target revision was attached to the comment in the report.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:12.820
The view contrasts with other firms that continue to flag remaining regulatory and scaling hurdles.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:19.000
An analyst report highlighted optimus humanoid robots as a potential major revenue contributor.

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:25.400
The note pointed to internal Tesla deployment as the initial proving ground before external sales.

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:29.620
No unit volume or pricing assumptions were detailed in the summary.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:35.800
The projection assumes successful scaling of the Gigatexus production line now under construction.

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:45.060
The base model Y rear wheel drive starts at $39,990 and removes some higher trim features.

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:51.900
Reviewers noted reduced sound insulation and simpler interior materials compared with long range versions.

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:55.740
The lower price targets buyers previously priced out of the lineup.

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:01.260
Real world range and charging performance remain consistent with other model Y variants.

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:07.060
On the product side, Tesla is also rolling out new software features for existing owners.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:11.920
Tesla is preparing to release actually smart summon for the Cybertruck.

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:17.880
The feature allows the vehicle to navigate parking lots and approach the owner without driver input.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:24.500
This follows earlier Cybertruck's specific software updates and comes ahead of broader unsupervised ambitions.

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:30.160
Owners will watch whether the system handles the truck's size and turning radius without additional

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:35.720
interventions. Tesla confirmed the summon feature for Cybertruck will begin rolling out in the near

00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:42.220
term. The update targets the same parking lot navigation use case. Owners are tracking whether the

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:49.120
truck's dimensions require any unique tuning. Eclipse showed the vehicle maintaining 69 to 70 miles per

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:56.080
hour in a 55 miles per hour zone while also staying in the left lane. The driver noted the behavior

00:05:56.080 --> 00:06:01.980
occurred on the standard setting rather than a more aggressive profile. The example illustrates how

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:08.420
speed compliance can vary even when drivers select conservative modes. Owners report the system moves

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:13.540
to the slower lane more readily when the fast lane is congested and the car is set to hurry.

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:19.040
The behavior appears tied to traffic density rather than a fixed preference for passing lanes.

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:24.200
It highlights how FSD interprets driver intent through the chosen profile.

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:31.020
Observers noted the current SpaceX valuation arguments echo the early skepticism Tesla faced.

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:36.840
The comparison underscores how long development timelines can test investor patients before

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:43.800
results appear. A new Tesla facility is under construction on the south end of Pancho Road in Camarillo.

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:48.640
The site appears separate from existing service or delivery centers in the area.

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:54.780
Local observers are watching for clues on whether it will support sales, service, or another function.

00:06:55.360 --> 00:07:00.520
Before we close, a quick look at the regulatory philosophy behind the supervised rollouts.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:07.780
Europe's incremental approvals for supervised FSD create a natural experiment in how regulators

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:14.240
weigh demonstrated miles against the absence of unsupervised capability. Denmark's decision

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:20.280
follows similar clearances in the Netherlands, Lithuania, and Estonia. Each requiring localized

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:26.660
safety data before drivers can activate the system. The pattern shows regulators accepting supervised

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:32.180
operation as a distinct category rather than demanding full autonomy from day one.

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:38.840
That approach differs from the US path where unsupervised robot taxi deployment remains the headline

00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:45.620
goal. In Europe, the supervised label keeps the driver legally responsible, which lowers the regulatory

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:52.300
bar but also caps the service model Tesla can offer. The distinction matters for gross margin because

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:58.680
supervised features still require a paid driver or owner behind the wheel, while true unsupervised

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:04.840
operation would shift the economics toward fleet utilization rates. The open variable is whether

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:10.520
the safety snapshots Tesla is now publishing will accelerate or slow further European expansion.

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:15.920
If localized data continues to show lower intervention rates than human drivers,

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:22.500
additional countries may follow the same supervised route. If the data instead highlights edge cases,

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:28.400
regulators could extend review periods and delay revenue from software subscriptions in those markets.

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:34.800
Tomorrow will be watching for further details on how localized safety data influences approvals

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:43.780
in additional European markets. And that's a wrap on today's Tesla news. TSLA closed at $396.68

00:08:43.780 --> 00:08:52.340
up 79 cents 0.2%. If you enjoyed this episode, please leave a rating or review. It genuinely helps other

